<title>USA: TABLE-Transfinancial Q2 net income up 94 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Transfinancial Q2 net income up 94 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LENEXA, Kan. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Months</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr		  $0.11		    $0.05</p>
<p> Net		  $704		     $362</p>
<p> Oper revs	  $32,775		  $28,345</p>
<p> Avg shrs	   6,320		    6,892</p>
<p>	  6 Months</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.21		    $0.10</p>
<p> Net		 $1,336		   $715</p>
<p> Oper revs	 $64,164		  $53,561</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  6,347		    7,014</p>
<p>(in thousands, except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Company says net income sharply higher on improved volumes and pricing in the transportation operation and lower cost of funds and administrative costs in the financial services business.</p>
<p>	    -- Company says on July 1 it effected a 1-for-100</p>
<p>reverse stock split followed by a 100-for-1 forward stock split.  The net effect of the stock splits was to cancel approximately 107,000 shares held by hodlers of less than 100 shares.</p>
</text>
